# The static-website pack's five keys — every repo-specific value the vendored
# release pipeline reads. Explicit on purpose: nothing is published, versioned,
# built or tested here except what this file names.
#
# The site is served from the repo root, so the publish set is the part of the
# root that is the site: the four pages, the two front-ends' code (js/ for the
# Now page, plan/ for the planner), the shared/ helpers both import, the css/,
# the data/ the app fetches, and package.json — which the debug pill fetches for
# the version. Everything else at the root is how the site is MADE, not part of
# it: scraper/, docs/, design-concepts/, plan/design/, product-wiki/, scripts/
# and the agent tooling were all served by the old whole-root upload and are
# deliberately not here.
publish_root=.
publish_paths=.nojekyll index.html accessibility.html privacy.html terms.html css js shared data package.json plan/index.html plan/plan.css plan/plan.js plan/lib

version_files=package.json

# Stamps js/build-info.js and injects the analytics beacon token — the two
# inline steps the hand-rolled deploy used to do, now run on pull requests too.
build_command=bash scripts/build-site.sh

# The repo's own gate: unit tests, JS/Python syntax, the normalizer self-test.
# The same script the pre-commit hook runs.
test_command=bash scripts/verify.sh
